From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhao <jerryz123@berkeley.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep TVM writable with Bare supervisor mode
Purpose: Separates architectural TVM writability from whether paging is available.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

TVM is read-only zero only when S-mode is absent. A Bare-only S-mode hart can
still use it to intercept satp and SFENCE.VMA accesses from supervisor mode.
Keep Spike's existing intercept checks and allow the bit to be written.

diff --git a/riscv/csrs.cc b/riscv/csrs.cc
index b60485b7..960d6fda 100644
--- a/riscv/csrs.cc
+++ b/riscv/csrs.cc
@@ -707,7 +707,7 @@ bool mstatus_csr_t::unlogged_write(const reg_t val) noexcept {
                    | MSTATUS_MPP
                    | (proc->extension_enabled('U') ? MSTATUS_TW : 0)
                    | (proc->extension_enabled('S') ? MSTATUS_TSR : 0)
-                   | (has_page ? MSTATUS_TVM : 0)
+                   | (proc->extension_enabled('S') ? MSTATUS_TVM : 0)
                    | (has_gva ? MSTATUS_GVA : 0)
                    | (has_mpv ? MSTATUS_MPV : 0)
                    | (proc->extension_enabled(EXT_SMDBLTRP) ? MSTATUS_MDT : 0)
